spans.s:
uṣṇīṣa,
(1) nt. (in Skt. also m.; = Pali uṇhīsa), in Skt. only turban; in cpd. uṣṇīṣa-śīrṣa(n) or -śiras(ka), 32d of the 32 lakṣaṇa, q.v. (Pali uṇhīsa-sīsa), acc. to Pali DN comm. 〔ii.452.1 ff.〕 having a head the size and shape of which makes it seem turbanned. But in BHS (and Pali) interpreted as having a head surmounted by an excrescence, whether a top-knot of hair, or a growth in the skull. So Tib. regularly (uṣṇīṣa = gtsug tor), e.g. on Mvy 〔236〕 uṣṇīṣa-śiraska-tā. Confirmed by Gv 〔401.26 ff.〕 mūrdhni cāsyoṣṇīṣam abhinirvṛttam abhūt, sujātaṃ samantaparimaṇḍalaṃ madhyābhinyastakeśālaṃkāraṃ koṭīśatasahasrapattraratnapadmasaṃdarśitaṃ samantāt samabhāgapratiṣṭhitam aparimitamahārghyatāpradhānamadhyam. Cf. also uṣṇi, apparently = uṣṇīṣa in this sense, and uṣṇiṣa. In comp. as one of the lakṣaṇa, LV 〔105.11〕; 〔432.13〕; Dharmas 〔83〕; Mv 〔i.227.3〕; 〔ii.30.6〕; 〔307.4〕; Bbh 〔376.7〕;
(2) m., one of ten Krodha: Dharmas 〔11〕;
(3) in Mmk 〔41.7〕 aṣṭau uṣṇīṣarājānaḥ are mentioned as to be depicted in a rite; their names, given 〔41.10—11〕, are Cakravartin, Uṣṇīṣa, Abhyudgatoṣṇīṣa, Sitātapatra, Jayoṣṇīṣa, Kamaloṣṇīṣa, Tejorāśi, Unnatoṣṇīṣa. They seem not to be related to the Krodha of Dharmas 〔11〕, tho the first two names also occur in that list. Nothing significant is said of them.
